"Let's go and find more information about Database Managements Systems (DBMS).", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "You're done!"}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Instructions</span>: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.</span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}]}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}]}], "type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Database Systems ", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 8, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 2, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A1.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about database systems. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Identify information about the history of software and its characteristics in simple spoken and written situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands key information in simple written and spoken texts about topics related to software programming and its history.  Recognizes basic ideas on programming concepts and programming history in both written and spoken passages.", "type": "secondary_1"}]}, {"content": "enpe7n1le02ob08re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Simple past Tense of the Verb 'to Be' in Questions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "We use the <strong>simple past tense</strong> of the <strong>verb to be</strong> to talk about situations in the past. Let's see how to create questions using those two grammatical elements.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When we want to use the <strong>simple past tense</strong> of the <strong>verb  to be</strong> for asking questions, we use the following structure:<br/><br/>  <div class=\"center_text\">Verb \u2018to be' in simple past + Subject + Complement</div><br/><br/>  Example: </br><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Were</span> the database management systems easy to work with during the 60's?</span><br/><br/> As you can see in the example above, when we ask a question, we place the verb before the subject.<br/><br/> When we have an information question (or w-h question), we place the interrogative adverb (or w-h word) before the <strong>verb to be.</strong> <br/><br/>  Example:</br> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">When</span> was the first database management system invented?</span><br/><br/>  Let's take a look at the conjugation of the verb to be:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Subject\\t</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Example</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Was I in the office last night?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You, They, We\\t\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Were you organizing data?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He, She, It\\t\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Was it difficult to understand the functioning of database management?</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "How was data managed in these models? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "How were the coming generations influenced by this paper? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Was this model called RDBMS?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "There + Verb 'to Be' in Simple Past Tense in Questions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "We use <strong>there was</strong> and <strong>there were</strong> to talk about the past existence of something. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When we want to know if something existed or not in the past, we can use <strong>there was</strong> or <strong>there were</strong> in the interrogative form.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: </br><strong><i>Were there</strong><u> many database models</u> after the 1970s?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Remember that when we ask a question, we place the verb before the subject. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "It is also important to remember that we use <strong>there was</strong> when the subject is singular.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: </br><strong><i>Was there</strong> a <u>standardized model</u> for database management?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "We use <strong>there were</strong> when the subject is plural.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: </br><strong><i>Were there </strong><u>several standardized models</u> for database management?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Was there someone who put these ideas into practice?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Were there any data management models during the first half of the 20th century?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Were there any innovations that made the data management process easier?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "innovation ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " something that is new and different from its predecessors  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Were there any innovations that made the data management process easier? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le02ob08aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "manage ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to control or work with something ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: How was data managed in these models?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le02ob08aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "sophisticated ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something that is complex and that has a high quality", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: After this, other developers decided to create more sophisticated data models. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le02ob08aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "attempt ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an effort for accomplishing or getting something done", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There were successful attempts for making this model for data management come true.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le02ob08aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": " relationship ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a connection or relation between two or more elements", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Most models used a hierarchical system that represented data relationships as a tree.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le02ob08aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "root node ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a topmost or bottom node in a tree data structure", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The program has to read the whole tree from the root node.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le02ob08aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "a)\tWhat other first database systems were there in the beginning of database systems? Look for information about it. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "b)\tMake a list of the ones you find.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "c)\tWrite the description of one that you consider important.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "d)\tShare your description with a classmate.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "\u274f\tI look for information about database systems.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "\u274f\tI make a list of database systems.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "\u274f\tI write a description of one database system. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "\u274f\tI share my work with a classmate.", "type": "text"}]}]}